// Title: Network Connection Initiated By Regsvr32.EXE
// Sigma ID: c7e91a02-d771-4a6d-a700-42587e0b1095
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Dmitriy Lifanov, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-25 | Modified: 2023-09-18
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1559.001, T1218.010
// Description: Detects a network connection initiated by "Regsvr32.exe"
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://pentestlab.blog/2017/05/11/applocker-bypass-regsvr32/
//   - https://oddvar.moe/2017/12/13/applocker-case-study-how-insecure-is-it-really-part-1/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_regsvr32_network_activity.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe"
